WEBVTT

00:00.433 --> 00:04.045
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.046 --> 00:07.113
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.114 --> 00:10.819
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.820 --> 00:13.574
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.575 --> 00:17.192
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.193 --> 00:20.562
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.563 --> 00:22.030
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.031 --> 00:23.498
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.499 --> 00:28.727
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.729 --> 00:36.176
What are you doing to Dad?

00:36.177 --> 00:38.245
What? I'm going to the grocery store.

00:38.246 --> 00:40.580
<i>Okay, you remember Memento? That.</i>

00:40.581 --> 00:42.016
Don't forget the cucumbers, Peter.

00:42.017 --> 00:43.717
All right. Where's that?

00:43.718 --> 00:46.086
Oh, hey, right, 'cause of
that thing we started doing.

00:46.087 --> 00:48.688
By the way, speaking of
which, best "O" ever.

00:48.689 --> 00:50.724
I felt dirty for an hour,
but it's gone now.

00:50.725 --> 00:52.192
Now I just can't wait for night.

00:52.193 --> 00:54.027
I wish you hadn't said
that at full volume

00:54.028 --> 00:56.021
in front of our children.

00:56.022 --> 00:58.232
I can't tell if they have
a really good marriage

00:58.233 --> 00:59.632
or a really bad one.

00:59.633 --> 01:01.916
I feel like it's weird but strong.

01:01.917 --> 01:03.370
Like Danny Trejo.

01:04.273 --> 01:05.757
Thank you for noticing.

01:11.462 --> 01:14.414
You ready for movie
marathon day, Rupert?

01:14.415 --> 01:16.583
Ah, I was born ready, too.

01:16.584 --> 01:18.452
<i>All right, time for Fast and the Furious</i>

01:18.453 --> 01:19.887
one through seven.

01:19.888 --> 01:22.122
All right, let's get (BLEEP) high.

01:22.123 --> 01:23.958
You can't be high for this, Brian.

01:23.959 --> 01:25.224
This is serious stuff.

01:25.225 --> 01:27.126
This is a 14-hour meditation

01:27.127 --> 01:29.729
on the importance of family, fast cars,

01:29.730 --> 01:32.777
product placement, racial
ambiguity and family.

01:33.619 --> 01:35.302
Where's eight? Didn't
that one just come out?

01:35.303 --> 01:37.471
<i>Someone said they were
going to get me eight</i>

01:37.472 --> 01:38.973
on Blu-ray for my birthday,

01:38.974 --> 01:41.275
<i>and someone got me a limited edition</i>

01:41.276 --> 01:43.977
Michael Kors pebbled
leather tote bag instead.

01:43.978 --> 01:45.964
- You love that bag.
- I know. You're the best.

01:45.965 --> 01:47.557
<i>Okay, put in Fast 6.</i>

01:47.558 --> 01:48.748
You're starting with six?

01:48.749 --> 01:51.418
Um, yeah. We're going in
order from best to worst.

01:51.419 --> 01:54.188
Six, five, seven, three... I
know that's controversial...

01:54.189 --> 01:55.789
One, four, two.

01:55.790 --> 01:57.024
By the way, don't tell Rupert

01:57.025 --> 01:58.993
about Paul Walker being D-E-A-D.

01:58.994 --> 02:00.087
He doesn't know.

02:02.447 --> 02:03.797
All right. So, what's the plot?

02:03.798 --> 02:06.934
Oh, you don't understand these movies.

02:09.037 --> 02:10.504
What was that, Rupert?

02:10.505 --> 02:11.715
Oh, yes.

02:12.540 --> 02:13.604
Yes.

02:14.141 --> 02:15.327
No.

02:15.943 --> 02:18.096
I don't know. Maybe? Maybe bi?

02:18.779 --> 02:21.279
That's Ludacris. That's not Tyrese.

02:21.280 --> 02:22.984
What are you talking about?
They look nothing alike.

02:22.985 --> 02:24.724
Ludacris looks like a human peanut,

02:24.725 --> 02:26.153
and Tyrese looks slick.

02:26.154 --> 02:27.941
He looks like a Chinese black.

02:27.942 --> 02:29.828
Like Africa and Asia had sex

02:29.829 --> 02:31.358
while Europe sat on a chair

02:31.359 --> 02:33.410
in the corner of the
hotel room and watched.

02:33.411 --> 02:36.030
Ludacris, human peanut.
Tyrese, Chinese black.

02:36.031 --> 02:37.998
Are you gonna keep talking like
this during the whole thing?

02:37.999 --> 02:39.806
What? I'm answering Rupert's questions.

02:39.807 --> 02:41.173
Now we're gonna have to rewind.

02:41.174 --> 02:43.637
We just missed the scene where
half the team steals a tank

02:43.638 --> 02:45.873
while the other half pretends
to be a DJ for some reason.

02:45.874 --> 02:47.206
- Damn it.
- Yeah, okay.

02:47.207 --> 02:49.043
- I'm going to the bar.
- Suit yourself.

02:49.044 --> 02:51.303
Rupert and I are just fine without you.

02:52.404 --> 02:53.479
You're right.

02:53.480 --> 02:54.914
I bet he is on his period.

02:54.915 --> 02:56.650
Whatever that means.

02:56.651 --> 02:58.052
La, la, la, la. Stop, stop, stop, stop.

02:58.053 --> 02:59.353
Gross, gross, gross. Ew, ew, ew.

02:59.354 --> 03:01.284
No, no, no. No. Ew. Ew.

03:01.285 --> 03:03.590
A loaf of bread, a container of milk

03:03.591 --> 03:05.592
and a stick of butter.

03:05.593 --> 03:07.928
A loaf of milk, a container of bread

03:07.929 --> 03:10.097
<i>and a Joe Dirt DVD.</i>

03:10.098 --> 03:12.699
<i>A Joe Dirt DVD, Scarlett Johansson</i>

03:12.700 --> 03:14.919
and treasure from a fish tank.

03:17.389 --> 03:18.906
<i> Attention, shoppers.</i>

03:18.907 --> 03:21.174
<i>Beloved cereal icon Boo Berry</i>

03:21.175 --> 03:23.494
<i>is now greeting customers in aisle six.</i>

03:23.495 --> 03:25.446
Boo Berry?

03:25.447 --> 03:26.747
<i>The Boo Berry?</i>

03:26.748 --> 03:28.749
<i>Are there imposter Boo Berries?</i>

03:28.750 --> 03:30.028
Hey, watch it.

03:31.069 --> 03:33.353
Oh, Mr. Boo Berry, I'm your biggest fan.

03:33.354 --> 03:34.955
You're not the one threatening me

03:34.956 --> 03:36.090
on Facebook, are you?

03:36.091 --> 03:39.126
No, no. No, not-not you. Not you.

03:39.127 --> 03:41.195
Hey, you know what I always
loved about your cereal?

03:41.196 --> 03:42.955
It tasted like blueberries.

03:42.956 --> 03:44.898
<i>Oh, my God. Boo Berries.</i>

03:44.899 --> 03:46.475
And you're... and you're a ghost.

03:46.476 --> 03:47.935
'Cause... So that-that's the "boo."

03:47.936 --> 03:50.271
Did you guys know you were
doing that? Oh, my God.

03:50.272 --> 03:52.440
- Anyway, can I shake your hand?
- Sure.

04:09.491 --> 04:11.892
I've been touched by greatness.

04:11.893 --> 04:14.561
I am never washing this hand again.

04:14.562 --> 04:16.262
This is the best thing to happen to me

04:16.263 --> 04:17.831
since I became a wisecracking,

04:17.832 --> 04:20.176
fourth-wall-breaking superhero.

04:20.177 --> 04:21.635
Call me Redstool.

04:21.636 --> 04:23.070
The treatment didn't give me powers,

04:23.071 --> 04:25.172
but it did spread cancer to my anus.

04:25.173 --> 04:27.785
♪ Just call me anus ♪

04:27.786 --> 04:29.327
♪ Of the morning ♪

04:29.328 --> 04:31.227
♪ Anus ♪

04:31.228 --> 04:33.180
♪ Just touch my cheek ♪

04:33.181 --> 04:35.572
♪ Before you leave me ♪

04:35.573 --> 04:37.783
♪ Anus ♪

04:37.784 --> 04:42.022
♪ This violence juxtaposed to music ♪

04:42.023 --> 04:43.656
♪ Anus ♪

04:43.657 --> 04:45.856
♪ Decapitation ♪

04:45.857 --> 04:48.342
♪ In slow-motion ♪

04:48.343 --> 04:50.290
♪ Anus. ♪

05:00.775 --> 05:03.093
Sorry, Rupert. I think
I'm down for the count.

05:03.094 --> 05:04.343
You okay if I go to bed?

05:04.344 --> 05:07.505
Oh, I like that we're comfortable
doing things separately, too.

05:07.506 --> 05:08.585
Good night.

05:08.586 --> 05:11.018
Do me a favor and don't wake
me when you come up, though.

05:11.019 --> 05:13.653
Yes, you do. You always
step on the creaky board.

05:13.654 --> 05:15.819
Yes, you do. Every time.

05:15.820 --> 05:17.901
<i>No, you're being a little bitch.</i>

05:19.410 --> 05:20.493
Don't go to bed angry.

05:20.494 --> 05:21.628
Don't go to bed angry.

05:21.629 --> 05:23.740
Defuse. Defuse.

05:24.307 --> 05:25.866
Rupert, I'm sorry.

05:25.867 --> 05:27.300
I overreacted.

05:27.301 --> 05:28.679
Now you say you're sorry.

05:28.680 --> 05:30.208
What do you mean, "For what"?

05:30.209 --> 05:31.258
I hate you!

05:34.370 --> 05:35.748
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

05:35.749 --> 05:37.578
I love you. I value you.

05:37.579 --> 05:39.312
We're not escalating. It's fine.

05:39.313 --> 05:40.980
I'll see you in the morning.

05:40.981 --> 05:42.092
Good night.

05:51.918 --> 05:53.994
<i> Hi, this is Vin Diesel.</i>

05:53.995 --> 05:56.396
<i>Welcome to the DVD menu.</i>

05:56.397 --> 05:58.232
<i>Why don't you grab yourself a Corona,</i>

05:58.233 --> 06:00.886
<i>hit play and enjoy the ride.</i>

06:01.863 --> 06:03.841
<i>Hi, this is Vin Diesel.</i>

06:03.842 --> 06:06.169
<i>Welcome to the DVD menu.</i>

06:06.170 --> 06:07.905
Oh, boy, you're hungover.

06:07.906 --> 06:09.750
How are you going to do nothing today?

06:13.631 --> 06:14.882
Oh, my God.

06:14.883 --> 06:16.301
Rupert?

06:23.605 --> 06:25.440
No! Rupert!

06:25.441 --> 06:28.978
Rupert!

06:28.979 --> 06:31.465
<i>Hi, this is Vin Diesel.</i>

06:31.466 --> 06:34.701
<i>Oh, man, did your friend
kill your other friend?</i>

06:34.702 --> 06:36.220
<i>That's betrayal.</i>

06:36.221 --> 06:37.899
<i>That's not strong.</i>

06:37.900 --> 06:40.206
<i>Danny Trejo is strong.</i>

06:40.207 --> 06:42.042
Aw. Come on, guys.

06:42.043 --> 06:43.758
This is getting embarrassing.

06:52.650 --> 06:53.868
Murderer!

06:53.869 --> 06:55.330
You killed Rupert.

06:55.331 --> 06:57.136
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

06:57.137 --> 06:58.497
Hey, whoa. Hey, what's going on?

06:58.498 --> 07:01.566
You killed my best friend
is what's going on.

07:01.567 --> 07:03.502
Oh. Uh-oh.

07:03.503 --> 07:04.936
Bear-killing bastard.

07:04.937 --> 07:07.506
Oh, my God. Stewie, I am so sorry.

07:07.507 --> 07:09.074
I-I was drunk. It was an accident.

07:09.075 --> 07:10.809
I must have thought he was a chew toy.

07:10.810 --> 07:12.978
So? If you were driving
drunk and ran him over,

07:12.979 --> 07:14.412
would you still go to jail?

07:14.413 --> 07:15.814
Yes! You killed him.

07:15.815 --> 07:17.249
Let me make it up to you, please.

07:17.250 --> 07:18.830
How about you kill something I love?

07:18.831 --> 07:20.117
How about I do that?

07:20.118 --> 07:21.996
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa, whoa. Okay.

07:21.997 --> 07:23.884
Okay, that's-that's fine. That's fair.

07:23.885 --> 07:25.357
No, I-I meant, like-like...

07:25.358 --> 07:26.825
like my favorite tennis ball.

07:26.826 --> 07:29.531
You're comparing Rupert
to a tennis ball?

07:29.532 --> 07:30.783
What is wrong with you?

07:30.784 --> 07:32.251
No wonder you two never got along.

07:32.252 --> 07:34.395
He always knew there was
something off about you,

07:34.396 --> 07:36.564
and now we know what it
was. You're a psycho!

07:36.565 --> 07:38.032
- Stewie, I didn't mean to...
- Shut up!

07:38.033 --> 07:40.134
- You don't understand. I...
- Shut up.

07:40.135 --> 07:42.702
Stop trying. It's over.

07:42.703 --> 07:44.238
Look at me. Watch. See what I'm doing?

07:44.239 --> 07:45.973
Twitter: unfollow.

07:45.974 --> 07:47.741
Instagram: unfollow.

07:47.742 --> 07:49.577
Snapchat: unfollow.

07:49.578 --> 07:51.645
And there we go. Done.

07:51.646 --> 07:53.347
We are not friends anymore.

07:53.348 --> 07:54.749
- But, Stewie...
- Bye.

07:54.750 --> 07:56.916
Dikembe Mutombo, will you do the thing?

07:56.917 --> 07:59.200
Brian, you are blocked.

08:08.424 --> 08:11.031
Why are you brushing your
teeth with your left hand?

08:11.032 --> 08:13.410
Can't risk the right getting wet, Lois.

08:13.411 --> 08:16.770
Boo Berry touched it, and it is now
a sacred space, like a temple.

08:16.771 --> 08:18.739
Okay. Well, I'm gonna
have middle-aged woman,

08:18.740 --> 08:21.509
boobs-falling-off-to-the-side sleep now.

08:29.201 --> 08:30.851
Hey, Chris, have you seen...

08:30.852 --> 08:32.952
What, uh... what-what are you doing?

08:32.953 --> 08:36.165
<i>Operating my thriving
quincea├▒era dress business.</i>

08:36.166 --> 08:37.758
Do me a favor, stand on that chair?

08:37.759 --> 08:40.226
Uh, okay.

08:40.227 --> 08:41.962
So, what's up?

08:41.963 --> 08:43.764
I'm looking for Stewie.
He and I had a fight,

08:43.765 --> 08:45.633
and I'm scared he might've
done something drastic.

08:45.634 --> 08:46.900
Him?

08:46.901 --> 08:48.468
You're the one who killed his friend.

08:48.469 --> 08:50.971
Okay, I see he got to you before I did.

08:50.972 --> 08:52.706
It's a stuffed animal, Chris.

08:52.707 --> 08:55.042
Yeah, well, he cremated
that stuffed animal,

08:55.043 --> 08:57.912
and he's going to Vermont
to scatter the ashes.

08:57.913 --> 08:59.613
What? I got to go after him.

08:59.614 --> 09:01.615
Not until I finish fitting this.

09:01.616 --> 09:03.451
<i>How you feeling? Bueno? Fits good?</i>

09:03.452 --> 09:04.543
This isn't mine.

09:04.544 --> 09:07.489
<i>Do you or do you not feel bonita?</i>

09:08.198 --> 09:09.323
<i>I feel bonita.</i>

09:09.324 --> 09:11.800
<i>Wonderful, because you look bonita.</i>

09:11.801 --> 09:15.847
<i>Gracias, cari├▒a, puedes
recogerlo el mi├йrcoles.</i>

09:16.816 --> 09:20.143
Pablo is gonna lose his mind.

09:21.136 --> 09:22.270
Mwah.

09:27.493 --> 09:28.676
Stewie!

09:28.677 --> 09:30.577
Hmm. Well, violent murderers

09:30.578 --> 09:32.111
can often be found at bus stations,

09:32.112 --> 09:33.313
so why am I surprised?

09:33.314 --> 09:34.981
You can't go to Vermont alone.

09:34.982 --> 09:36.842
I'm not. Got Rupert with me.

09:36.843 --> 09:38.284
He and I had an agreement,

09:38.285 --> 09:41.154
if he died first, I would scatter
his ashes on a mountain.

09:41.155 --> 09:43.524
If I died first, he would
throw my body whole

09:43.525 --> 09:45.125
into the fountain at the Bellagio.

09:45.126 --> 09:46.660
I don't care. I'm coming with you.

09:46.661 --> 09:48.095
Well, you're not going to sit with me.

09:48.096 --> 09:49.697
Oh, come on. If I don't, I'll get stuck

09:49.698 --> 09:51.448
next to that guy with the heavy hands.

09:51.449 --> 09:53.100
Hi, doggy.

09:54.336 --> 09:55.719
Serves you right.

09:55.720 --> 09:57.004
And a baby.

10:26.042 --> 10:27.642
I can hear you following me.

10:27.643 --> 10:29.181
- Good.
- I swear to God,

10:29.182 --> 10:30.538
do not take one step further,

10:30.539 --> 10:32.091
<i>or I will hit you.</i>

10:33.323 --> 10:34.341
That's it!

10:35.370 --> 10:38.156
Leave! Me! Alone! Murderer!

10:38.157 --> 10:39.513
Stewie, stop! Stop, all right?

10:39.514 --> 10:42.057
Look, why are you being such
a jerk over a stupid bear?

10:42.058 --> 10:44.051
Don't you disrespect the dead!

10:49.518 --> 10:50.558
Aah!

10:53.028 --> 10:54.028
Aah!

10:55.781 --> 10:57.948
He's not dead! He was never alive!

10:57.949 --> 10:59.296
You take those words back!

10:59.297 --> 11:01.669
He wouldn't care! He didn't
hear them! He's a doll!

11:01.670 --> 11:03.121
He was my best friend!

11:04.338 --> 11:06.465
<i>I'm supposed to be your best friend.</i>

11:06.466 --> 11:07.507
Well, you're not!

11:07.508 --> 11:10.002
You're a bloodthirsty,
cold-hearted murderer!

11:10.003 --> 11:11.345
Fine. You're right.

11:11.346 --> 11:12.963
You know what? It wasn't an accident.

11:12.964 --> 11:14.631
I knew he wasn't a chew toy.

11:14.632 --> 11:16.550
I was sick of you talking
to him all the time.

11:16.551 --> 11:18.452
I was sick of you
complaining to him about me

11:18.453 --> 11:19.720
when I'm right there in the room.

11:19.721 --> 11:22.690
And I was sick of always playing
second fiddle to that bear!

11:22.691 --> 11:24.918
He's not even real!

11:25.627 --> 11:27.094
You did it...

11:27.712 --> 11:29.214
on purpose?

11:40.213 --> 11:41.451
Stewie!

11:43.785 --> 11:45.363
Oh, my God, Stewie!

11:47.995 --> 11:49.918
Ah, I didn't know we were blowing it up.

11:58.426 --> 11:59.743
Rupert! Where...

11:59.744 --> 12:00.824
Oh, there you are.

12:01.413 --> 12:03.304
- Stewie, you're hurt.
- It's just my ankle.

12:03.305 --> 12:05.483
- It's not a big deal.
- It's already swelling up.

12:05.484 --> 12:07.051
- Just let me...
- Back off!

12:07.052 --> 12:09.085
I'm doing this on my own. For Rupert.

12:12.440 --> 12:14.749
Damn it, Stewie, just...

12:14.750 --> 12:16.219
just sit there, will ya?

12:16.220 --> 12:17.403
I'll-I'll get us up.

12:18.895 --> 12:20.498
I didn't want your help.

12:20.499 --> 12:22.117
Well, you need it, so it's happening.

12:25.787 --> 12:27.805
This isn't going to make
me forgive you, you know.

12:27.806 --> 12:28.823
That's fine.

12:28.824 --> 12:30.441
I'm going to say uncomplimentary things

12:30.442 --> 12:33.243
- about your ass the whole way.
- Go ahead.

12:33.244 --> 12:35.847
You know, maybe it's appropriate
that you're my ride up.

12:35.848 --> 12:38.081
Rupert always called you my "bitch."

12:38.082 --> 12:40.017
Want to know some of the
other things he called you?

12:40.018 --> 12:41.419
Fat Lassie.

12:41.420 --> 12:42.753
Scooby-Don't.

12:42.754 --> 12:44.121
Rin Tin Twink.

12:44.122 --> 12:45.355
Poopy Snoopy.

12:45.356 --> 12:46.990
Marma-dookie.

12:46.991 --> 12:49.660
Clifford the Big Red Sphincter
That We See All the Time

12:49.661 --> 12:51.662
Because You Don't Put Your Tail Down.

12:51.663 --> 12:53.616
Snoop Doggy Dick.

12:57.237 --> 12:58.237
Hey, guys.

13:04.359 --> 13:06.944
- What the hell is that?
- My Boo Berry hand.

13:06.945 --> 13:08.546
I swore I'd never wash it again,

13:08.547 --> 13:10.113
even though Lois keeps telling me to.

13:10.114 --> 13:11.549
You should listen to her.

13:11.550 --> 13:13.117
Yeah, Peter, that's disgusting.

13:13.118 --> 13:15.121
- Oh, yeah? Take that!
- Aah!

13:15.122 --> 13:17.301
That started happening yesterday.

13:17.302 --> 13:19.557
To the bathroom!

13:19.558 --> 13:21.291
We got to get him to wash that hand.

13:21.292 --> 13:22.693
Yeah. I'll text Lois,

13:22.694 --> 13:24.695
see if we can't all
come up with something.

13:24.696 --> 13:26.363
Just reply to that last GIF she sent

13:26.364 --> 13:28.165
of the sloth putting on the headphones.

13:29.401 --> 13:30.902
I love that one.

13:30.903 --> 13:32.837
Is it weird that we're in a group text

13:32.838 --> 13:34.872
with our friend's wife
but not our friend?

13:34.873 --> 13:37.375
No, what's weird is that
your Bitmoji can walk.

13:37.376 --> 13:40.411
I'm allowed to have legs
in the phone world!

13:47.232 --> 13:50.105
You know, once we're done here,
I'm never speaking to you again.

13:50.106 --> 13:51.738
Well, how the hell was
I supposed to know

13:51.739 --> 13:53.039
it was gonna upset you so much?

13:53.040 --> 13:55.075
How? How?!

13:55.076 --> 13:57.632
You saw me spend almost
every single minute

13:57.633 --> 14:00.380
of every single day with
Rupert since I was born!

14:00.381 --> 14:02.141
And you don't... up-up,
hang on, hang on.

14:02.142 --> 14:03.167
Another hiker going by.

14:03.168 --> 14:04.835
One of us is going the wrong way. Heh.

14:04.836 --> 14:07.704
Ha-ha-ha! When are they gonna
put in the elevator, right?

14:07.705 --> 14:08.805
Ha-ha-ha.

14:08.806 --> 14:09.840
I loved Rupert!

14:09.841 --> 14:11.776
He was the most important
thing in my life,

14:11.777 --> 14:14.111
and you willfully violated
the sanctity and trust

14:14.112 --> 14:16.247
of our friendship when
you destroyed him!

14:16.248 --> 14:18.690
Stewie... I just don't get it.

14:18.691 --> 14:20.611
You're so mature in so many ways.

14:20.612 --> 14:22.353
You're... you're the smartest
person in the house.

14:22.354 --> 14:24.104
You're incredibly perceptive.

14:24.105 --> 14:26.823
You're wiser than people
40 times your age.

14:26.824 --> 14:29.776
Why is Rupert the one baby
thing you're hanging onto?

14:29.777 --> 14:31.511
Why are you so upset over a doll

14:31.512 --> 14:33.246
when I'm real and I'm still here?

14:33.247 --> 14:35.874
Because Rupert was going
to be with me forever!

14:35.875 --> 14:37.835
He wasn't ever going to leave!

14:38.945 --> 14:41.046
So what? I'm not leaving you, either.

14:41.047 --> 14:43.006
Oh, really? Brian, let's be honest.

14:43.007 --> 14:44.382
You're a middle-aged dog.

14:44.383 --> 14:46.051
You don't have that many years left.

14:46.052 --> 14:48.637
And one day, all too soon,
I'm gonna be crying

14:48.638 --> 14:50.376
at your funeral in an Armani suit,

14:50.377 --> 14:52.268
and people are gonna be
like, "Oh, nice suit,"

14:52.269 --> 14:53.674
and I'm gonna be like,
"Why are you talking

14:53.675 --> 14:56.786
about my awesome $2,000
suit... my friend's dead!"

14:56.787 --> 14:58.122
Feels like that story is less about me

14:58.123 --> 14:59.490
and more about your suit.

14:59.491 --> 15:01.691
Go to hell! Besides,
if you don't believe

15:01.692 --> 15:04.261
Rupert was real, why are
you so jealous of him?

15:04.262 --> 15:06.797
Why does it bother you how upset I am?

15:06.798 --> 15:07.864
That...

15:07.865 --> 15:09.599
is a very good point.

15:09.600 --> 15:12.703
Damn right it is, you joyless,
fake-wisdom-spouting...

15:12.704 --> 15:15.539
Hey. Heh. When are they gonna put
in the elevator, right? Heh.

15:15.540 --> 15:17.808
Yeah. That other guy said that to me.

15:17.809 --> 15:19.068
Nice shorts.

15:23.865 --> 15:25.849
For the record, I would have preferred

15:25.850 --> 15:27.550
to dress as Frankenburry.

15:27.551 --> 15:29.884
- That doesn't make any sense.
- And this does?

15:29.885 --> 15:31.722
If anything, we all three should've been

15:31.723 --> 15:33.490
Snap, Crackle and Pop.

15:33.491 --> 15:36.576
Yeah, we missed an opportunity there.

15:36.577 --> 15:38.395
- It's fine.
- We did this wrong!

15:38.396 --> 15:40.689
Joe, it's fine. It's...
Cleveland, just ring the bell.

15:41.691 --> 15:43.816
Oh, I wonder who that could be.

15:43.817 --> 15:44.886
I'll get it.

15:47.155 --> 15:49.919
- Oh, my God!
- Count Chocula!

15:49.920 --> 15:51.074
That's right.

15:51.075 --> 15:54.978
Silly rabbit, Count
Chocula tastes grrreat!

15:54.979 --> 15:57.714
Oh, it's an honor to meet you, sir.

15:58.917 --> 16:00.918
Aah!

16:00.919 --> 16:03.020
- Wh-What's happening?
- We got you, Peter.

16:03.021 --> 16:04.855
Yeah, there's a golf
ball scrubber in there.

16:04.856 --> 16:06.145
Just relax and let it happen.

16:06.146 --> 16:07.758
No! No!

16:07.759 --> 16:10.412
My miraculous tiny life-forms!

16:28.063 --> 16:29.680
Where are we going, Father?

16:29.681 --> 16:32.116
To a place better than this, son.

16:33.635 --> 16:35.285
Yay!

16:48.483 --> 16:50.601
Well, Rupert, we made it.

16:50.602 --> 16:51.953
It's beautiful up here.

16:52.937 --> 16:55.221
So should... should we just...

16:55.222 --> 16:57.040
sprinkle him around randomly, or...?

16:57.041 --> 16:59.610
Oh, don't be a savage,
Brian. What is your problem?

16:59.611 --> 17:01.464
We have to have the ceremony first.

17:02.831 --> 17:04.555
Dearest Rupert,

17:04.556 --> 17:05.647
we're here.

17:06.494 --> 17:08.285
I never wanted this to happen,

17:08.286 --> 17:10.703
and it happened far, far too soon.

17:10.704 --> 17:11.955
But...

17:11.956 --> 17:13.187
I can't.

17:14.092 --> 17:15.959
You... you do it.

17:15.960 --> 17:17.227
Wha... What?

17:17.228 --> 17:20.097
You give the eulogy. I'm
too upset. I can't.

17:20.098 --> 17:21.632
What am I supposed to say?

17:21.633 --> 17:24.067
I don't know, Just...
just tell the truth.

17:24.068 --> 17:27.638
Let-let Rupert know how important he is.

17:27.639 --> 17:29.458
Okay, um...

17:30.458 --> 17:31.975
Rupert was...

17:31.976 --> 17:33.977
a-a great bear,

17:33.978 --> 17:36.413
uh, a great, uh...

17:36.414 --> 17:38.782
- Power bottom.
- Right, right, okay.

17:38.783 --> 17:42.653
But most importantly of
all, he was a great friend.

17:42.654 --> 17:45.355
He was always there
whenever Stewie needed him.

17:45.356 --> 17:47.524
He was understanding.

17:47.525 --> 17:48.781
He always listened.

17:49.362 --> 17:51.287
He made Stewie a better person.

17:52.555 --> 17:53.597
Stewie...

17:54.333 --> 17:55.967
and I are both...

17:56.434 --> 17:59.436
incredibly grateful for all
the time we had with you,

17:59.437 --> 18:02.039
and we wouldn't change a single moment.

18:02.040 --> 18:03.774
Except the end.

18:03.775 --> 18:04.975
Sorry about that.

18:04.976 --> 18:07.445
Um, rest in peace, Rupert.

18:17.872 --> 18:19.498
Thank you, Brian.

18:20.291 --> 18:21.333
That was...

18:21.893 --> 18:23.294
that was beautiful.

18:25.296 --> 18:28.198
♪ How do I ♪

18:28.199 --> 18:31.134
♪ Say good-bye ♪

18:31.135 --> 18:35.030
♪ To what we had? ♪

18:35.686 --> 18:37.945
♪ The good times ♪

18:37.946 --> 18:40.744
♪ That made us laugh ♪

18:40.745 --> 18:44.366
♪ Outweigh the bad ♪

18:46.368 --> 18:48.010
♪ I thought ♪

18:48.820 --> 18:51.944
♪ We'd get to see forever ♪

18:52.798 --> 18:55.425
♪ But forever's ♪

18:55.426 --> 18:58.220
♪ Gone away ♪

18:58.863 --> 19:01.698
♪ It's so hard ♪

19:01.699 --> 19:04.959
♪ To say good-bye ♪

19:04.960 --> 19:08.338
- ♪ To yesterday ♪
- ♪ To yesterday... ♪

19:08.339 --> 19:10.172
♪ Go up there, Brian. ♪

19:10.173 --> 19:12.609
Okay, Brian, now pour it out.

19:12.610 --> 19:14.813
- What?
- Pour it out, whatever you have.

19:14.814 --> 19:15.946
Pour it out.

19:15.947 --> 19:18.358
I have a Gatorade bottle
full of pee from the bus.

19:18.359 --> 19:20.075
Pour it out for Rupert.

19:32.814 --> 19:35.699
- ♪ I don't know ♪
- ♪ Ooh... ♪

19:35.700 --> 19:37.267
♪ Where this road ♪

19:37.268 --> 19:39.803
You're with Paul now, Rupert!

19:39.804 --> 19:41.405
- ♪ Is going ♪
- ♪ Ooh, ooh ♪

19:41.406 --> 19:43.825
- ♪ To lead ♪
- ♪ Ooh... ♪

19:46.061 --> 19:48.779
♪ All I know ♪

19:48.780 --> 19:52.582
♪ Is where we've been ♪

19:52.583 --> 19:54.818
♪ And what we've been through ♪

19:54.819 --> 19:56.486
♪ Ooh... ♪

19:56.487 --> 19:58.506
♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh ♪

19:59.841 --> 20:02.092
♪ If we get ♪

20:02.093 --> 20:04.928
♪ To see tomorrow ♪

20:04.929 --> 20:06.730
♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪

20:06.731 --> 20:09.165
♪ I hope it's worth ♪

20:09.166 --> 20:11.000
♪ All the wait ♪

20:11.001 --> 20:13.136
♪ Ah, ah... ♪

20:13.137 --> 20:16.273
♪ It's so hard ♪

20:16.274 --> 20:17.474
♪ To say good-bye ♪

20:17.475 --> 20:19.343
♪ Bye ♪

20:19.344 --> 20:20.777
♪ To yesterday ♪

20:20.778 --> 20:23.013
♪ Day... ♪

20:24.515 --> 20:27.020
Rupert! You've come back to me!

20:27.021 --> 20:29.753
♪ And I'll take ♪

20:29.754 --> 20:32.856
♪ With me the memories ♪

20:32.857 --> 20:34.190
♪ The memories ♪

20:34.191 --> 20:36.626
♪ To be my sunshine ♪

20:36.627 --> 20:38.846
♪ After the rain ♪

20:40.180 --> 20:43.000
♪ It's so hard ♪

20:43.001 --> 20:46.303
♪ To say good-bye ♪

20:46.304 --> 20:47.838
♪ To yesterday ♪

